{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.LambdaScaleSubstrateForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.LambdaScaleSubstrateForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_all_c_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_all_c_i","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L111-L122","doc":"**Summary of all c_i for Family A** (closed-form theorem):\n\nλ_A(q) = 5/2 + (3/4)·h² + 0·h⁴ + 0·h⁶ + ...\n\nThe series terminates exactly. All odd h-coefficients vanish\nby q ↔ q⁻¹ symmetry. All even h^{2k} coefficients for k ≥ 2\nvanish by the closed-form expression. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_q_inv_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_q_inv_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L98-L109","doc":"**Theorem (q ↔ q⁻¹ symmetry)**: λ_A is invariant under q → 1/q.\n\nThis implies all ODD h-coefficients vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_higher_even_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_higher_even_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L89-L96","doc":"**Theorem c_{2k} for k ≥ 2 (= 0)**: all higher even h-coefficients\nvanish.  The h-series is exactly polynomial of degree 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_c4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_c4","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L79-L87","doc":"**Theorem c_4 (= 0)**: there is no h⁴ term in λ_A.\n\nThe h-series is polynomial of degree 2, so the h⁴ coefficient is\nidentically zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_c2","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L72-L77","doc":"**Theorem c_2**: the h² coefficient in λ_A is exactly 3/4.\n\nFollows directly from `lambdaA_hForm h = 5/2 + (3/4)·h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_c0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_c0","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L67-L70","doc":"**Theorem c_0**: at q = 1, λ_A = 5/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_qForm_eq_hForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_qForm_eq_hForm","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L54-L65","doc":"**Theorem (Family A closed form).** The two forms are equal:\n`λ_A(q) = 5/2 + (3/4)·h(q)²`.\n\nProof: algebraic substitution h² = q² − 2 + q⁻². ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:lambda-scale-substrate-form","label":"prop:lambda-scale-substrate-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_hForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_hForm","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L50-L52","doc":"The same Family A substrate-form expressed in `h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_qForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaA_qForm","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L41-L48","doc":"The natural Family A substrate-form for λ_scale at H_4,\nin q-rational form.\n\n`λ_A(q) = (3q² + 4 + 3q⁻²) / 4 = (1/4) · Σ_λ dim_q V_λ`\nwhere the sum runs over the 5 partitions of 4 with quantum\ndimensions {1, [3]_q, [4]_q/[2]_q, [3]_q, 1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeDeformation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeDeformation","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lambda-scale-substrate-form.lean#L38-L39","doc":"The Hecke deformation `h(q) = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}